    {
      "title": "Module 1 \u00b7 Prisms & Cylinders",
      "html": "<ul><li>Cube: $V=a^3$; SA $=6a^2$.</li><li>Cuboid: $V=lbh$; SA $=2(lb+bh+lh)$.</li><li>Cylinder: $V=\\pi r^2 h$; total SA $=2\\pi r(r+h)$.</li></ul><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$V = a^3 = 5^3 = 125\\ \\text{cm}^3$.</li><li>$SA = 6a^2 = 6\\times 64 = 384\\ \\text{cm}^2$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the volume of a cube of side $5$ cm.<br/><b>A:</b> 125 \\text{ cm}^3</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the total surface area of a cube of side $8$ cm.<br/><b>A:</b> 384 \\text{ cm}^2</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Find the volume of a cylinder with $r=7$ cm, $h=10$ cm (take $\\pi=22/7$).",
          "a": "$V = \\tfrac{22}{7}\\times 49\\times 10 = 1540\\ \\text{cm}^3$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 2 \u00b7 Cones, Spheres, Pyramids",
      "html": "<ul><li>Cone: $V=\\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h$; slant $l=\\sqrt{r^2+h^2}$; curved SA $=\\pi r l$.</li><li>Sphere: $V=\\tfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3$; SA $=4\\pi r^2$.</li><li>Pyramid: $V=\\tfrac{1}{3}(\\text{base area})\\times h$.</li></ul><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$V = a^3 = 5^3 = 125\\ \\text{cm}^3$.</li><li>$SA = 6a^2 = 6\\times 64 = 384\\ \\text{cm}^2$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the volume of a cube of side $5$ cm.<br/><b>A:</b> 125 \\text{ cm}^3</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the total surface area of a cube of side $8$ cm.<br/><b>A:</b> 384 \\text{ cm}^2</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Volume of a sphere with $r=3$ cm (take $\\pi=22/7$).",
          "a": "$V = \\tfrac{4}{3}\\times \\tfrac{22}{7}\\times 27 = \\tfrac{2376}{21} \\approx 113.14\\ \\text{cm}^3$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 3 \u00b7 Frustums",
      "html": "<p>A frustum is what remains after cutting the top off a cone (or pyramid) with a plane parallel to the base.</p>$$V_{\\text{frustum}} = \\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi h(R^2 + Rr + r^2)$$<h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$V = a^3 = 5^3 = 125\\ \\text{cm}^3$.</li><li>$SA = 6a^2 = 6\\times 64 = 384\\ \\text{cm}^2$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> Find the volume of a cube of side $5$ cm.<br/><b>A:</b> 125 \\text{ cm}^3</p><p><b>Q:</b> Find the total surface area of a cube of side $8$ cm.<br/><b>A:</b> 384 \\text{ cm}^2</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "State the frustum volume formula.",
          "a": "$V=\\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi h(R^2 + Rr + r^2)$ where $R$, $r$ are the radii of the two circular faces and $h$ is the perpendicular distance between them."
        }
      ]
    },
